                "**Fear of loss** — People may fear job loss, reduced status, loss of competence, comfortable routines or identity. Loss aversion means a $500 upside with a status downside can feel like a loss.",
                "**Uncertainty and lack of information** — People often tolerate known bads better than unknowns. Information vacuums fill with worst-case rumours.",
                "**Genuinely better knowledge** — Frontline resistors may be right that the new process breaks a real constraint. Dismissing resistance loses valuable frontline intelligence.",
                "**Vested interests** — People who profit from the status quo may resist rationally, such as a middle manager whose layer the restructure deletes.",
                "**Change fatigue and distrust** — If the last three changes were badly run, resistance may be a rational response, as shown by the veteran’s ‘we tried this in 2019’.",
