              text: "Advantage decays through three mechanisms. **Imitation** occurs when rivals copy what works, such as imitators appearing within a year after a successful bubble tea shop opens. **Erosion** occurs when the trend that carried the advantage moves on (15.3). **Neglect** occurs when quality drifts as the owner's attention does, creating the consistency problem described in 8.3."
