                "**Financial over-extension** — debt service goes beyond what quiet months can carry; the overdraft is used for expansion; working capital is stripped to fund the second site; or a personal guarantee is sized for the *best* scenario. The signature is that the business is profitable on paper and insolvent by Thursday.",
                "**Capacity over-extension** — sales are promised beyond operations’ ability to deliver. For example, a caterer accepts the 300-guest wedding with a 150-guest kitchen: the revenue is real, and so is the reputational ruin. Quality can dilute under load, as with the second café breaking the first one’s standards, while delivery times lengthen as volume grows.",
                "**Management over-extension** — the owner becomes the bottleneck at scale. The founder now “runs” three sites and actually runs none; decisions queue behind one tired person.",
